[{"POLYGON":"43.656735,-79.379779,\r\n43.656648,-79.379738,\r\n43.65657,-79.379739,\r\n43.656557,-79.37975,\r\n43.656542,-79.379799,\r\n43.656516,-79.379808,\r\n43.656487,-79.379858,\r\n43.656489,-79.379873,\r\n43.656485,-79.379879,\r\n43.656484,-79.379923,\r\n43.656549,-79.380195,\r\n43.656537,-79.3802,\r\n43.656552,-79.380262,\r\n43.656537,-79.380345,\r\n43.656525,-79.380347,\r\n43.656518,-79.380358,\r\n43.656529,-79.380397,\r\n43.656525,-79.380423,\r\n43.65651,-79.380424,\r\n43.656499,-79.380473,\r\n43.656502,-79.38049,\r\n43.656475,-79.380581,\r\n43.656484,-79.380597,\r\n43.656479,-79.380696,\r\n43.65651,-79.380698,\r\n43.656516,-79.380751,\r\n43.656525,-79.380758,\r\n43.65654,-79.380815,\r\n43.65655,-79.380814,\r\n43.656552,-79.380822,\r\n43.656574,-79.380821,\r\n43.656577,-79.380825,\r\n43.656623,-79.380823,\r\n43.656697,-79.380736,\r\n43.656691,-79.380721,\r\n43.656701,-79.380724,\r\n43.656759,-79.380463,\r\n43.656759,-79.380463,\r\n43.656869,-79.380502,\r\n43.65691,-79.3805,\r\n43.656937,-79.380382,\r\n43.656912,-79.380374,\r\n43.656915,-79.380357,\r\n43.656831,-79.380312,\r\n43.656913,-79.379942,\r\n43.656715,-79.37985,","DETAILS":"Located on the northeast corner of Dundas Square, DSQ has its entrance on Dundas St. between Yonge St. and Victoria St. It also has internal links to the Dundas Station subway stop and PATH via the lower levels.\n<br/><br/>\nIn addition to the Cineplex Cinemas Yonge-Dundas, which provide TMU with lecture spaces, the office tower at the southeast corner of the building provides space for Zone Education and other research facilities.","ACCESSIBILITY":"DSQ has internal links to the Dundas Station, which is the nearest accessible subway station to TMU.\n<br/><br/>\nThe main entrance has a barrier-free approach and doors with automated operators. \n<br/><br/>\nThe office tower elevators serve TMU spaces on Levels 4 through 10. The cinemas and third-floor DMZ space can be accessed via the main public elevators.\n<br/><br/>\nTMU spaces on the 3rd floor have single-occupancy washrooms with accessibility features. The other floors have washroom stalls with accessibility features.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.656518, -79.380493","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Yonge-Dundas Square","CENTER":"43.656738,-79.380239","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/sy5RlBeac9o","CODE":"DSQ","HOURS":"Access to Toronto MU spaces in this building is only permitted with an authorized OneCard.","ADDRESS":"10 Dundas Street East","ID":"13","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657368,-79.37974,\r\n43.657413,-79.379734,\r\n43.657441,-79.379602,\r\n43.657177,-79.379497,\r\n43.657145,-79.379653,","DETAILS":"The Chang School building is immediately south of Devonian Pond (a.k.a. \"Lake Devo\") and its main entrance is on Victoria St. beneath historical Art Deco relief sculptures. \r\n\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nCED is home to the administrative offices of The Chang School of Continuing Education and has some conference facilities on upper floors.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance can be accessed via a sloped sidewalk (ramp) or exterior stairs and has an automatic sliding door that is available during business hours. A secondary entrance with a barrier-free approach and automated door operator is also available on the north side of the building under the overhang by Lake Devo.\n<br/><br/>\nWashrooms have stalls with accessibility features. \n<br/><br/>\nThe elevators are near the reception area.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657185, -79.379723","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"The Chang School of Continuing Education – Heaslip House","CENTER":"43.657285,-79.379614","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/P6kTGxDj_0o","CODE":"CED","HOURS":"Monday to Thursday | 8:15 a.m. to 6:45 p.m.<br/>\nFriday | 8:15 a.m. to 4:15 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"297 Victoria Street","ID":"18","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657206,-79.378516,\r\n43.657232,-79.378385,\r\n43.65722,-79.37838,\r\n43.657258,-79.3782,\r\n43.657203,-79.378177,\r\n43.65722,-79.378098,\r\n43.657106,-79.378046,\r\n43.657018,-79.37848,\r\n43.657111,-79.378525,\r\n43.657131,-79.378525,\r\n43.657139,-79.378501,\r\n43.657185,-79.378517","DETAILS":"BON is an administrative building with offices for employees involved in university safety operations. Access is restricted to operational personnel only.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance is level with the sidewalk and has a door operator.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657100, -79.378509","ELEVATOR":"no","NAME":"111 Bond Street","CENTER":"43.657157,-79.378294","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"BON","HOURS":"24 hours a day, 7 days a week","ADDRESS":"111 Bond Street","ID":"20","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.658967,-79.375741,\r\n43.658995,-79.375622,\r\n43.659031,-79.375636,\r\n43.659039,-79.375635,\r\n43.659042,-79.375598,\r\n43.659002,-79.375582,\r\n43.659012,-79.375541,\r\n43.658758,-79.37543,\r\n43.65871,-79.375428,\r\n43.658661,-79.375603,\r\n43.658608,-79.37558,\r\n43.658601,-79.375579,\r\n43.6585,-79.376042,\r\n43.658577,-79.376073,\r\n43.658576,-79.376089,\r\n43.658586,-79.376099,\r\n43.658612,-79.376093,\r\n43.658612,-79.376088,\r\n43.658713,-79.376131,\r\n43.658718,-79.376129,\r\n43.658744,-79.376003,\r\n43.658748,-79.376007,\r\n43.658754,-79.376004,\r\n43.658766,-79.375947,\r\n43.658778,-79.375947,\r\n43.65882,-79.375758,\r\n43.658873,-79.375776,\r\n43.658881,-79.375775,\r\n43.658901,-79.375714,\r\n43.658967,-79.375741","DETAILS":"The ILC is a former hotel that was converted into a student residence and conference centre. Its main entrance fronts on the west side of Jarvis St. midway between Gerrard St. East and Dundas St. \n<br/><br/>\nIt has a second entrance on the west side of the building at 133 Mutual St. that is more commonly used by students to access the TMU campus.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The Mutual St. entrance (43.658594, -79.376091) has an accessibility ramp from the sidewalk and an automated door operator. \n<br/><br/>\nThere is a single-occupancy washroom with accessibility features available off the main corridor of the second floor.\n<br/><br/>\nElevators are across from the concierge desk by the Jarvis St. main entrance.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.658779, -79.375458","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"International Living/Learning Centre","CENTER":"43.658779,-79.375641","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/j9pI1qIQJa4","CODE":"ILC","HOURS":"<b>133 Mutual St</b><br/>\nMonday to Friday |  6:30 a.m. to 11 p.m.<br/>\r\nSaturday | 6:30 a.m. to 11 p.m.<br/>\r\nSunday | 6:30 a.m. to 11:59 p.m.<br/><br/>\r\n<b>240 Jarvis</b><br/>\n24 hours a day, 7 days a week<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"133 Mutual Street","ID":"24","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657418,-79.380425,\r\n43.657585,-79.380498,\r\n43.657655,-79.380188,\r\n43.657577,-79.380166,\r\n43.657483,-79.380129,","DETAILS":"The Campus Store has a corner entrance facing the pedestrianized plaza at Gould St. and Victoria St. south of the Library Building. It sells textbooks and other course materials as well as TMU apparel and merchandise.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The Campus Store entrance is level with the plaza and the building has an automated door operator.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657593, -79.380192","ELEVATOR":"no","NAME":"Campus Store","CENTER":"43.65755,-79.380295","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/qKrGL7RNbHU","CODE":"BKS","HOURS":"Monday to Thursday | 9 a.m. to 6:30 p.m.<br/>\r\nFriday | 9 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.<br/><br/>\r\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard.\r Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"17 Gould Street","ID":"26","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657557,-79.378174,\r\n43.657548,-79.378174,\r\n43.657494,-79.378418,\r\n43.657478,-79.378412,\r\n43.65747,-79.378412,\r\n43.657415,-79.378654,\r\n43.657605,-79.378736,\r\n43.657614,-79.378737,\r\n43.657709,-79.378309,\r\n43.65771,-79.378305,\r\n43.657687,-79.378291,\r\n43.657707,-79.378203,\r\n43.65769,-79.378195,\r\n43.657664,-79.378171,\r\n43.657648,-79.378164,\r\n43.657557,-79.378174","DETAILS":"HEI is on the east side of Bond St., 40 metres south of Gould St. \n<br/><br/>\nThe building is the main facility for the School of Graphic Communications Management.","ACCESSIBILITY":"HEI’s main entrance has a barrier-free approach and an automated door operator. Washrooms have stalls with accessibility features. \n<br/><br/>\nThe elevator is at the far end of the corridor that runs along the windows of the north side of the building.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657587, -79.378695","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"School of Graphic Communications Management – Heidelberg Centre","CENTER":"43.657572,-79.378447","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/m7HDPnXfFSk","CODE":"HEI","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 7 a.m. to 8:30 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday | 8 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change","ADDRESS":"125 Bond Street","ID":"28","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.65441586992685,-79.38263587653637,\r\n43.654467296406075,-79.38241727650166,\r\n43.65384241318424,-79.38215710222721, \r\n43.65381718484309,-79.38215978443623, \r\n43.65371821201768,-79.38189424574375,\r\n43.6539239200602,-79.38173867762089,\r\n43.653973406323765,-79.38151203095913,\r\n43.6536561113381,-79.3813819438219,\r\n43.65363379389069,-79.3813806027174,\r\n43.65332620040098,-79.38161127269268,\r\n43.653181621213264,-79.38226975500584,\r\n43.653216553129425,-79.38226841390133,\r\n43.65327574327434,-79.38222415745258,\r\n43.653369865187884,-79.38247628509998,\r\n43.653289327889524,-79.38253797590733,\r\n43.65407334904542,-79.38286520540714,\r\n43.65411507265674,-79.38286252319813,\r\n43.65441586992685,-79.38263587653637","DETAILS":"TMU has research space in the building that sits between Bay Street, near City Hall and the Eaton Centre. The entrance at the corner of Albert Street and James Street is nearest the TMU facilities and is easily reached by travelling through the Eaton Centre.\n<br/><br/>\nBTS is home to the Responsive Ecologies Lab (RE/Lab).","ACCESSIBILITY":"Building entrance doors have automatic door operators and the TMU facilities are on the first floor.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.653491, -79.381510","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Bell Trinity Square","CENTER":"43.653626,-79.382256","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"BTS","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"483 Bay Street","ID":"142","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657557,-79.378173,\r\n43.657548,-79.378174,\r\n43.6573,-79.378068,\r\n43.657299,-79.378045,\r\n43.657389,-79.377644,\r\n43.657398,-79.377644,\r\n43.657664,-79.377757,\r\n43.657627,-79.377929,\r\n43.657557,-79.378173","DETAILS":"SID is on the west side of Church St. a short distance for pedestrians travelling south from Gould St. The main entrance to the vintage building has a step up from the sidewalk. \n<br/><br/>\nThe School of Interior Design is the only building occupant and makes use of its flexible studio workshop and classroom spaces","ACCESSIBILITY":"An entrance with accessibility features is available on the west side of the building (GPS 43.657483, -79.378142) via a laneway from Bond St. immediately south of the School of Graphic Communications Management (HEI) by 125 Bond St. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nAll washrooms in the building are single-occupancy and all-gender. There is a washroom with accessibility features on each floor.\n<br/><br/>\nThe elevator is in the main entrance lobby of the building.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657571, -79.377711","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"School of Interior Design","CENTER":"43.657456,-79.377894","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/aV1ehZ74oWg","CODE":"SID","HOURS":"Monday to Thursday | 8:30 a.m. to 7 p.m. <br/>\nFriday | 8:30 a.m. to 5 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.<br/>\nWest entrance entry is only permitted with authorized OneCard access.","ADDRESS":"302 Church Street","ID":"27","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.655602,-79.383498,\r\n43.655647,-79.383496,\r\n43.655908,-79.382301,\r\n43.655271,-79.382038,\r\n43.655251,-79.38203,\r\n43.65516,-79.382458,\r\n43.655133,-79.382462,\r\n43.654967,-79.383233,","DETAILS":"TRS is on the south side of Dundas St. with its main entrance mid-way between Bay St. and Yonge St. \n<br/><br/>\nThe building has retail tenants below TMU spaces on levels 7 through 9. The TMU occupied floors are labelled TRS-1, TRS-2 and TRS-3 and can be accessed by escalators or elevators from the main lobby.\n<br/><br/>\nThe Ted Rogers School of Management has most of its operations in the building. There are also event spaces.","ACCESSIBILITY":"TRS has a barrier-free approach and the rightmost door has an automated door operator.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThere is a single-occupancy, all-gender washroom with accessibility features on each floor. The main washrooms also have stalls with accessibility features. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nIn addition to the main elevator lobby, there is an elevator in the southwest corner of the building that travels between TMU floors.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.655803, -79.382657","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Ted Rogers School of Management","CENTER":"43.655407,-79.382787","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/60fuv4KZnqg","CODE":"TRS","HOURS":"Monday to Thursday | 7:30 a.m. to 10 p.m.<br/>\nFriday and Saturday | 7:30 a.m. to 6:30 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"575 Bay Street (entrance at 55 Dundas Street West)","ID":"25","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.659569,-79.382122,\r\n43.659829,-79.38225,\r\n43.659945,-79.382242,\r\n43.660039,-79.381859,\r\n43.659757,-79.381725,\r\n43.659666,-79.381726","DETAILS":"YNG is an office tower on the east side on Yonge St. a short distance for pedestrians travelling north from Gerrard St. \n<br/><br/>\nTMU has offices for University Advancement and University Relations in the building.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance has an accessibility ramp from the sidewalk and an automated door operator.\n<br/><br/>\nFloors 3, 12 and 18 have single-occupancy, all-gender washrooms for TMU spaces.\n<br/><br/>\nThe elevators are in the main lobby.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.659716, -79.382191","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"415 Yonge Street","CENTER":"43.659916,-79.382042","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"YNG","HOURS":"Access to Toronto MU spaces in this building is only permitted with an authorized OneCard.","ADDRESS":"415 Yonge Street","ID":"31","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657285,-79.378055,\r\n43.657377,-79.377631,\r\n43.656757,-79.377377,\r\n43.656666,-79.377778,\r\n43.657285,-79.378055","DETAILS":"The DCC is on the west side of Church St. just north of Dundas St. The main entrance is at 288 Church St. It opens into the north atrium where there is a security desk and the elevator lobby. \n<br/><br/>\nThere are two intercoms at the main entrance connecting to TMU Security and the residence reception desk respectively.\n<br/><br/>\nThe public parking vehicle entrance can be accessed from the laneway at the south end of the building. Visitors parking at the DCC who do not carry OneCards must use the TMU Security intercom at the main entrance to return to their vehicles.\n<br/><br/>\nThe academic portion of the facility is primarily the home to: Daphne Cockwell School of Nursing, School of Occupational and Public Health, School of Nutrition and Midwifery Education Program.\n<br/><br/>\nIt also provides facilities for the Design + Technology Lab, Learning and Teaching Centre and Graduate Studies.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The DCC was awarded gold standard accessibility certification from the Rick Hansen Foundation. \n<br/><br/>\nAll entrances, classrooms and labs have barrier-free approaches and automated door operators and there are tactiles warning surfaces by stairs. Assistive listening technology is available in classrooms, labs and seminar rooms.\n<br/><br/>\nEach floor has a single-occupancy, barrier-free washroom and larger washrooms also have stalls with accessibility features. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nThe main elevator lobby provides service for the parking and academic levels. A second set of elevators provides service for the residence tower.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657341, -79.377596","ELEVATOR":"no","NAME":"Daphne Cockwell Health Sciences Complex","CENTER":"43.657104,-79.377724","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"DCC","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"288 Church Street","ID":"101","WHEELCHAIR":"no"},{"POLYGON":"43.65976,-79.389572,\r\n43.659459,-79.389439,\r\n43.659536,-79.389095,\r\n43.659112,-79.388914,\r\n43.658951,-79.389622,\r\n43.659673,-79.389932,\r\n43.65976,-79.389572","DETAILS":"TMU has space in the MaRs Discovery Centre West tower, which fronts on University Ave. at the College St. intersection. The building’s concourse level has links to the TTC Queen’s Park Station.\n<br/><br/>\nThe building has purpose-built laboratory facilities for TMU’s Faculty of Science on the 11th floor.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The west tower has an automated door operator at the main entrance from University Ave. and elevator access to the TMU facilities on the 11th floor.\n<br/><br/>\nWashrooms have stalls with accessibility features.\n<br/><br/>\nThe building has links to the accessible Queen’s Park subway station.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.659584, -79.389893","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"MaRS Building","CENTER":"43.659374,-79.389524","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"MRS","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"661 University Ave","ID":"83","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657877,-79.379989,\r\n43.657905,-79.379987,\r\n43.658177,-79.379793,\r\n43.658227,-79.3795,\r\n43.658238,-79.379487,\r\n43.65824,-79.37946,\r\n43.658229,-79.379438,\r\n43.658225,-79.379435,\r\n43.658243,-79.379404,\r\n43.658236,-79.379356,\r\n43.658193,-79.379347,\r\n43.658206,-79.379295,\r\n43.65823,-79.379294,\r\n43.65824,-79.379254,\r\n43.658256,-79.379259,\r\n43.658253,-79.37927,\r\n43.658284,-79.379274,\r\n43.658298,-79.379233,\r\n43.658308,-79.379232,\r\n43.658319,-79.379123,\r\n43.658271,-79.379113,\r\n43.658309,-79.378924,\r\n43.658303,-79.378918,\r\n43.658306,-79.378906,\r\n43.658298,-79.378904,\r\n43.658323,-79.378788,\r\n43.658345,-79.378798,\r\n43.658372,-79.378798,\r\n43.658378,-79.37878,\r\n43.658396,-79.378782,\r\n43.658467,-79.37847,\r\n43.658469,-79.378458,\r\n43.658308,-79.378083,\r\n43.65829,-79.378079,\r\n43.658281,-79.378152,\r\n43.658262,-79.378161,\r\n43.658143,-79.378706,\r\n43.658162,-79.378725,\r\n43.658135,-79.378837,\r\n43.658123,-79.378839,\r\n43.658119,-79.378864,\r\n43.65811,-79.378864,\r\n43.658041,-79.379207,\r\n43.658045,-79.379208,\r\n43.658042,-79.379224,\r\n43.658049,-79.379233,\r\n43.658023,-79.379352,\r\n43.658011,-79.379353,\r\n43.658003,-79.379382,\r\n43.657999,-79.379381,\r\n43.657962,-79.379565,\r\n43.657957,-79.379565,\r\n43.657947,-79.379616,\r\n43.657906,-79.3796,\r\n43.657885,-79.379597,\r\n43.657871,-79.379648,\r\n43.657856,-79.379657,\r\n43.657853,-79.379709,\r\n43.657847,-79.379707,\r\n43.657831,-79.379704,\r\n43.657809,-79.379738,\r\n43.657809,-79.379766,\r\n43.657834,-79.379784,\r\n43.657824,-79.379824,\r\n43.657834,-79.379828,\r\n43.657833,-79.379886,\r\n43.657882,-79.379895,\r\n43.657865,-79.379982","DETAILS":"KHS is along Gould St. from Nelson Mandela Walk (formerly Victoria St.) to Church St. Its Lower Ground and 1st floors are interrupted by a pair of archways to the Kerr Hall Quad.\n<br/><br/>\nThe eastern section of KHS can be accessed from an entrance under the east archway at 50 Gould St. that opens into a stairwell. The western section of KHS can be accessed from an entrance under the west archway at 40 Gould St.\n<br/><br/>\nKHS has several classrooms, labs, studio spaces and administrative offices such as Early Childhood Studies, Fashion, Creative Industries, and the Chemical Engineering and Mathematics departments.","ACCESSIBILITY":"Entrances with accessibility features from Kerr Hall North (KHN), Kerr Hall East (KHE) and Kerr Hall West (KHW) provide access to KHS via shared corridors and elevators at the east and west corners of the building. \n<br/><br/>\nThe service ramps at the 40 Gould St. entrance and 60 Gould St. loading area are not recommended for pedestrian travel.\n<br/><br/>\nWashroom stalls with accessibility features are on the 2nd floor and Lower Ground floor of the west portion. Single-occupancy washrooms with accessibility features are in the east half of Kerr Hall North which can be accessed via shared corridors. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.658079, -79.379421","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Kerr Hall South","CENTER":"43.658195,-79.37912","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/Rx4mqpVCHh4","CODE":"KHS","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 6 a.m. to 10:30 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday | 8 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"50 Gould Street","ID":"33","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657877,-79.379989,\r\n43.657905,-79.379987,\r\n43.658177,-79.379793,\r\n43.65839,-79.379883,\r\n43.658405,-79.379815,\r\n43.658419,-79.379814,\r\n43.65847,-79.379837,\r\n43.658474,-79.379824,\r\n43.658485,-79.379824,\r\n43.658493,-79.379824,\r\n43.658491,-79.37984,\r\n43.658501,-79.379844,\r\n43.658513,-79.379844,\r\n43.658535,-79.379856,\r\n43.658545,-79.379854,\r\n43.658668,-79.379921,\r\n43.658688,-79.379921,\r\n43.658814,-79.379977,\r\n43.658817,-79.379956,\r\n43.65883,-79.379956,\r\n43.658934,-79.38,\r\n43.658929,-79.380027,\r\n43.659059,-79.380083,\r\n43.659081,-79.380091,\r\n43.659286,-79.380593,\r\n43.659243,-79.380589,\r\n43.657874,-79.380007","DETAILS":"KHW runs along the east side of Nelson Mandela Walk (formerly Victoria St.) between Gerrard St. East and the Gould St. pedestrian plaza. Its main entrance is near the north end of the building facing Jorgenson Hall. A secondary entrance is at the centre of the building. \n<br/><br/>\nThe building can also be accessed using the centre entrance from the Kerr Hall Quad.\n<br/><br/>\nIt has internal links to the Library Building and Jorgenson Hall from pedestrian bridges on the 2nd and 3rd floors and a tunnel to Jorgenson Hall on the Lower Ground floor. All sections of Kerr Hall can be accessed via the second floor.\n<br/><br/>\nIt most notably is home to the Upper and Lower Gymnasiums on the 2nd floor and Lower Ground floor respectively, as well as TMU's Medical Centre and the Early Learning Centre of the 1st floor.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main and secondary entrances both have accessibility ramps and automated door operators.\n<br/><br/>\nWashroom stalls with accessibility features are on the 2nd floor and Lower Ground floor of Kerr Hall South. A single-occupancy washroom with accessibility features is available on the 2nd floor of Library Building by the accessible elevator and can be accessed via the pedestrian bridge. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nThe building shares elevators with Kerr Hall North and Kerr Hall South.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.659277, -79.380501","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Kerr Hall West","CENTER":"43.658742,-79.380161","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/Rx4mqpVCHh4","CODE":"KHW","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 6 a.m. to 10:30 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday | 8 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"379 Victoria Street","ID":"2","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.661684,-79.380783,\r\n43.661745,-79.380806,\r\n43.661767,-79.380808,\r\n43.66182,-79.38083,\r\n43.66183,-79.380816,\r\n43.661912,-79.38085,\r\n43.661914,-79.380869,\r\n43.662327,-79.38104,\r\n43.662367,-79.381042,\r\n43.662384,-79.38105,\r\n43.662416,-79.38105,\r\n43.662467,-79.381067,\r\n43.662699,-79.379956,\r\n43.662689,-79.379949,\r\n43.662715,-79.379823,\r\n43.66266,-79.379799,\r\n43.662661,-79.379789,\r\n43.66206,-79.379544,\r\n43.662052,-79.379543,\r\n43.661994,-79.379519,\r\n43.661959,-79.379518,\r\n43.661931,-79.379654,\r\n43.661922,-79.379654,\r\n43.661861,-79.379938,\r\n43.661831,-79.379938,\r\n43.661745,-79.380335,\r\n43.66177,-79.380348,\r\n43.661733,-79.380525,\r\n43.661737,-79.380529,\r\n43.661684,-79.380783,","DETAILS":"The MAC is located in the historic Maple Leaf Gardens, former home of the Toronto Maple Leafs. The building offers state-of-the-art athletic facilities including an NHL-sized ice arena, gymnasium and fitness centre. The MAC entrance is just west of Church St. on the north side of Carlton St., beneath the historic awning.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The TMU entrance has an automated door operator into the first floor lobby.\n<br/><br/>\nSingle-occupancy, barrier-free, all-gender washrooms and change spaces are available. \n<br/><br/>\nElevators are available from the west side of the first-floor lobby and serve all floors of the MAC","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.661827, -79.380149","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Mattamy Athletic Centre","CENTER":"43.662257,-79.380306","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/nhmk4Ez1qfE","CODE":"MAC","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 6 a.m. to 11:30 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday and Sunday | 7 a.m. to 11:30 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"50 Carlton Street","ID":"61","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.65957,-79.378155,\r\n43.659593,-79.378155,\r\n43.659665,-79.377828,\r\n43.65936,-79.377691,\r\n43.659339,-79.37769,\r\n43.659317,-79.377783,\r\n43.659143,-79.377709,\r\n43.65914,-79.377698,\r\n43.65917,-79.377689,\r\n43.659154,-79.3776,\r\n43.659142,-79.377599,\r\n43.659089,-79.377628,\r\n43.659079,-79.377629,\r\n43.65906,-79.377724,\r\n43.659081,-79.377723,\r\n43.659058,-79.377821,\r\n43.659062,-79.377824,\r\n43.659042,-79.377906,\r\n43.659016,-79.378025,\r\n43.659332,-79.378159,\r\n43.659352,-79.378158,\r\n43.659369,-79.378068","DETAILS":"The Architecture Building fronts on the east side of Church Street, just south of Gerrard St. East. It has a street-facing main entrance at the top of an outdoor staircase. A secondary key entrance on the east side of the building has accessibility features. \n<br/><br/>\nThe building is the home of the Architectural Science program and the Paul H. Cocker Gallery.","ACCESSIBILITY":"For an accessible route to the secondary entrance on the east side of the building, approach the building from the south and via the Pitman Quad. The east entrance has a barrier-free approach and an automated door operator\n<br/><br/>Washrooms on the 2nd floor have stalls with accessibility features.\n<br/><br/>There is an elevator in the east section of the building. Visitors can reach the gallery by taking the elevator to the second floor.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.659287, -79.377781","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Architecture Building","CENTER":"43.659229,-79.377927","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/qVKjJVEcY-w","CODE":"ARC","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 7:30 a.m. to 7:30 p.m \r\n<br/>\r<br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard.\r Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"325 Church Street","ID":"11","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657592,-79.37944,\r\n43.657603,-79.379434,\r\n43.657682,-79.379065,\r\n43.657689,-79.379064,\r\n43.657828,-79.379122,\r\n43.657747,-79.37949,\r\n43.657712,-79.379491,\r\n43.657592,-79.37944","DETAILS":"The Image Centre is a research centre and public gallery for photography and related arts. Its main entrance is at the northwest corner of the building next to Devonian Pond (a.k.a. \"Lake Devo\") along the pedestrianized boulevard of Gould St.\n<br/><br/>\nIt shares its building footprint and loading facilities with the School of Image Arts (IMA). \n<br/><br/>","ACCESSIBILITY":"The public entrance by Lake Devo has a barrier-free approach and an automated door operator.\n<br/><br/>\nWashrooms with accessibility features are in the connected Image Arts (IMA) building.\n<br/><br/>\nThe public gallery is on the first floor.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657699, -79.379539","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"The Image Centre","CENTER":"43.657716,-79.379261","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"IMC","HOURS":"Monday | Closed<br/>\nTuesday, Thursday and Friday | 11 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/>\nWednesday | 11 a.m. to 8 p.m. <br/>\nSaturday and Sunday | 12 p.m. to 5 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"33 Gould Street\nToronto ON M5B 1W1","ID":"3","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.658331,-79.377703,\r\n43.658554,-79.377797,\r\n43.658585,-79.377796,\r\n43.658589,-79.377792,\r\n43.658602,-79.377797,\r\n43.658636,-79.377799,\r\n43.658676,-79.377783,\r\n43.658718,-79.377754,\r\n43.658741,-79.377711,\r\n43.658762,-79.377663,\r\n43.658764,-79.377579,\r\n43.658736,-79.377497,\r\n43.658697,-79.37745,\r\n43.658667,-79.377433,\r\n43.658669,-79.377426,\r\n43.658627,-79.37741,\r\n43.658652,-79.3773,\r\n43.658872,-79.377393,\r\n43.658903,-79.37739,\r\n43.659053,-79.3767,\r\n43.658617,-79.376522,\r\n43.658588,-79.376518,\r\n43.658439,-79.377212,\r\n43.658569,-79.377267,\r\n43.658547,-79.377377,\r\n43.658445,-79.377334,\r\n43.658414,-79.377334,","DETAILS":"The RCC is at the northeast corner of the Gould St. and Church St. intersection. Its main entrance is on Gould St. 40 metres east of the corner. \n<br/><br/>\nIt can also be accessed from the second floor of Kerr Hall East using the pedestrian bridge over Church Street.\n<br/><br/>\nThe building is the main facility of the School of Journalism, the RTA School of Media, The Catalyst and the Dean’s office of The Creative School.","ACCESSIBILITY":"An accessibility ramp abuts the building along Gould St. to reach the main entrance at 80 Gould St. A secondary entrance is available from the Pitman Quad. Both entrances have automated door operators that open into an atrium between the east and west sections of the building.\n<br/><br/>\nAn all-gender, single-occupancy washroom with accessibility features is on the first floor of the east section of RCC. Stalls with accessibility features are available in other washrooms. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nThe elevator is in the east portion of the building close to the entrance atrium.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.658534, -79.377306","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Rogers Communications Centre","CENTER":"43.658705,-79.377036","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/IXCL5ZicMVg","CODE":"RCC","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 7 a.m. to 10 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday | 7:30 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"80 Gould Street","ID":"8","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.6616840,-79.3818185,\r\n43.6616840,-79.3818185,\r\n43.6617849,-79.3813679,\r\n43.6617849,-79.3813679,\r\n43.6615598,-79.3812686,\r\n43.6615598,-79.3812686,\r\n43.6614628,-79.3817487,\r\n43.6614628,-79.3817487,\r\n43.6615366,-79.3817756,\r\n43.6615366,-79.3817756,\r\n43.6615269,-79.3818024,\r\n43.6615269,-79.3818024,\r\n43.6616219,-79.3818265,\r\n43.6616219,-79.3818265,\r\n43.6616239,-79.3818051,\r\n43.6616239,-79.3818051,\r\n43.6616821,-79.3818212,\r\n43.6616821,-79.3818212,\n43.6616840,-79.3818185","DETAILS":"Imagine Cinemas’ downtown Carlton Cinema is on the north side of Carlton Street, a short distance for pedestrians travelling eastbound from the intersection of Yonge St. and College/Carlton St.\n<br/><br/>\nDuring the daytime hours, the cinemas provide TMU with lecture hall spaces and then functions as a movie theatre in the evenings. Students, faculty and staff are required to present their OneCards to theatre staff to enter during the class time hours.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The cinema has a ramp by the main entrance and an automatic door opener to access the main lobby.\n<br/><br/>\nThere is a single-occupancy washroom with accessibility features.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.661510, -79.381570","ELEVATOR":"","NAME":"Carlton Cinema","CENTER":"43.6616064,-79.3815529","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"CAR","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"20 Carlton Street","ID":"153","WHEELCHAIR":""},{"POLYGON":"43.656855,-79.378917,\r\n43.656814,-79.378899,\r\n43.656854,-79.37875,\r\n43.65689,-79.378766,\r\n43.656855,-79.378917","DETAILS":"BND is an administrative building with offices for employees that work in university operations. Access is restricted to operational personnel only.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The building was constructed in the 1860s and has original entryway features. There are stairs at the entrances and at this time there is no elevator to access the upper floors.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.656830, -79.378737","ELEVATOR":"no","NAME":"112 Bond Street","CENTER":"43.656863,-79.37883","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"BND","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"112 Bond Street","ID":"29","WHEELCHAIR":"no"},{"POLYGON":"43.660119,-79.376888,\r\n43.660151,-79.376735,\r\n43.659849,-79.3766,\r\n43.659842,-79.3766,\r\n43.659808,-79.376754,\r\n43.660112,-79.376887","DETAILS":"The 101 Gerrard Street East building is on the southeast corner of Gerrard St. and Mutual St. The building is one of two that are slated for redevelopment.\n<br/><br/>\nMechanical and Industrial Engineering research spaces are in the building.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance requires a step up from the sidewalk and there is no automation for the door.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.660128, -79.376758","ELEVATOR":"no","NAME":"101 Gerrard Street East","CENTER":"43.659921,-79.376732","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"COP","HOURS":"Access to Toronto MU spaces in this building is only permitted with an authorized OneCard.","ADDRESS":"101 Gerrard Street East","ID":"30","WHEELCHAIR":"no"},{"POLYGON":"43.659151,-79.381235,\r\n43.659213,-79.381232,\r\n43.659284,-79.380901,\r\n43.659269,-79.380892,\r\n43.659271,-79.380882,\r\n43.659072,-79.380797,\r\n43.65898,-79.380795,\r\n43.658906,-79.381131,","DETAILS":"The office tower of JOR is on the south side of Gerrard St. East, a short distance for pedestrians travelling eastward from Yonge St. Its main entrance is 40 metres south of the Gerrard St. sidewalk and fronts on Nelson Mandela Walk (formerly Victoria St.) facing Kerr Hall West.\n<br/><br/>\nThe JOR tower has the administrative offices of the Faculty of Arts and several of its departments. It is also the home of the university’s administration and operations departments and executive leadership.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance has an automated door operator and it is served by two accessibility ramps from the Gerrard St. sidewalk and Nelson Mandela Walk respectively.\n<br/><br/>\nThere is a universal washroom with an adult change table on the 14th floor and a single-occupancy washroom with accessibility features on the 1st floor off the main lobby. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"blank\">View washroom details<a/>).\n<br/><br/>\nThe elevator lobby for the office tower can be accessed via a corridor off the right side of the main lobby.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.658926, -79.380802","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Jorgenson Hall","CENTER":"43.659094,-79.380984","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/mQPlPB30oDw","CODE":"JOR","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 6 a.m. to 10 p.m.\r<br/>\nSaturday | 7:30 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/><br/>\r\r\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"380 Victoria St","ID":"6","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.6496155,-79.3776289,\r\n43.6493438,-79.3775189,\r\n43.6493438,-79.3775189, \r\n43.6493749,-79.3773606,\r\n43.6493749,-79.3773606,\r\n43.6496485,-79.3774787,\r\n43.6496155,-79.3776289, \r\n43.6496155,-79.3776289","DETAILS":"Magnet is a not-for-profit social innovation platform co-founded at TMU. The program has offices on the 7th floor of the 10 King East office tower.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The building has an automated door operator and elevators to the 7th floor.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"","ELEVATOR":"","NAME":"10 King Street East","CENTER":"43.6494933,-79.3774948","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"MAG","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"10 King Street East","ID":"154","WHEELCHAIR":""},{"POLYGON":"43.658375,-79.37927,\r\n43.658417,-79.379289,\r\n43.658428,-79.379285,\r\n43.658467,-79.379104,\r\n43.658428,-79.379088,\r\n43.658413,-79.379088,\r\n43.658375,-79.37927,","DETAILS":"The RAC is an underground athletics facility beneath the Kerr Hall Quad. Its main entrance is located at the preserved heritage façade of the Toronto Normal School at the south end of the Kerr Hall Quad at the top of a set of exterior stairs. \n<br/><br/>\nThe RAC has a pool, track, fitness centre, squash courts, training studios and more.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The accessible entrance is via the Kerr Hall North (KHN) 31 Gerrard St. East door (GPS 43.659277, -79.380501) can be reached by taking the KHN elevator to the Lower Ground level and following signage past the swimming pool viewing gallery to the RAC’s north entrance.\n<br/><br/>\nThere is a single-occupancy washroom with accessibility features by the reception desk and change spaces with showers are available.\n<br/><br/>\nThe RAC has an elevator at the south end of the facility.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.658356, -79.379185","ELEVATOR":"no","NAME":"Recreation and Athletics Centre","CENTER":"43.65843,-79.379171","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/hzHALKNwPlc","CODE":"RAC","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 6:30 a.m. to 10:30 p.m.<br/>\r\nSaturday | 9:30 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/>\r\nSunday |  9:30 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/>\r<br/>\nHours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"40 Gould Street","ID":"7","WHEELCHAIR":"no"},{"POLYGON":"43.65999,-79.377446,\n43.659457,-79.377223,\r\n43.659926,-79.377723,\r\n43.659914,-79.377726,\r\n43.659901,-79.377794,\r\n43.659862,-79.377795,\r\n43.659811,-79.377784,\r\n43.659779,-79.377784,\r\n43.659749,-79.377772,\r\n43.659753,-79.377748,\r\n43.659379,-79.377598,\r\n43.659382,-79.377583,\r\n43.659376,-79.377581,\r\n43.659381,-79.377562,\r\n43.659342,-79.377548,\r\n43.659346,-79.37753,\r\n43.659341,-79.377512,\r\n43.659359,-79.377448,\r\n43.65938,-79.377448,\r\n43.659432,-79.377216,\r\n43.659457,-79.377223","DETAILS":"EPH is on the south side of Gerrard St. East only 50 metres east of Church St. Its main entrance has two sets of double-doors at the top of an exterior staircase.\n<br/><br/>\nEPH provides facilities for engineering departments, Mathematics and the School of Social Work.","ACCESSIBILITY":"Barrier-free access to EPH is via the shared main entrance of Sally Horsfall Eaton Centre for Studies in Community Health (SHE) at 99 Gerrard St. East or the southwest EPH entrance from the Pitman Hall Quad across from the Architecture Building.\n<br/><br/>\nThere are single-occupancy washrooms with accessibility features on the 1st and 3rd floors. Other floors have washroom stalls with accessibility features. \n(<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nThe EPH passenger elevator is in the northwest corner of the building.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.659334, -79.377592","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Eric Palin Hall","CENTER":"43.659664,-79.37754","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/3I9LwBZx2zI","CODE":"EPH","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 6 a.m. to 10 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday | 9 a.m. to 5 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"87 Gerrard Street East","ID":"9","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657592,-79.37944,\r\n43.657603,-79.379434,\r\n43.657682,-79.379065,\r\n43.657612,-79.379034,\r\n43.657613,-79.379025,\r\n43.657621,-79.379026,\r\n43.657631,-79.378987,\r\n43.657543,-79.378952,\r\n43.657522,-79.378953,\r\n43.657516,-79.378988,\r\n43.657529,-79.378994,\r\n43.657529,-79.378999,\r\n43.657156,-79.378841,\r\n43.65713,-79.37884,\r\n43.65713,-79.378843,\r\n43.657102,-79.378845,\r\n43.657087,-79.37892,\r\n43.657075,-79.378917,\r\n43.657062,-79.378978,\r\n43.657097,-79.378995,\r\n43.65705,-79.379214","DETAILS":"IMA is on the west side of Bond St. at Gould St. \n<br/><br/>\nThe building is home to the various multimedia studios, event and exhibitions spaces of the School of Image Arts and shares space with its neighbour, The Image Centre, at 33 Gould St.\n<br/><br/>\nBalzac's Coffee Roasters is located at the north end of the building with a separate entrance from Gould St. across from Kerr Hall.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The building’s main entrance is near the intersection with a sloped sidewalk to the main doors, which have an automated door operator. A secondary entrance at the south end of the building also has a barrier-free approach and an automated door operator. \n<br/><br/>\nThere is a single-occupancy washroom with accessibility features on each floor. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nPassenger elevators are on the east side of the building near the main entrance.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657704, -79.379043","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"School of Image Arts","CENTER":"43.657445,-79.379158","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/i6yScO1bO30","CODE":"IMA","HOURS":"Monday, Tuesday Wednesday and Friday | 7:30 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/>\nThursday | 7:30 a.m. to 10 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday | 8 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"122 Bond Street","ID":"81","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.65672856248208,-79.38128152862191,\r\n43.656719344878624,-79.38128186389804,\r\n43.65669824141271,-79.3812962807715,\r\n43.656597332783484,-79.38174722716212,\r\n43.65632128859965,-79.38163524493575,\r\n43.656289754473285,-79.38163558021188,\r\n43.65590455165453,-79.3833957798779,\r\n43.65595379371433,-79.38341522589326,\r\n43.65597756572875,-79.3834906630218,\r\n43.65596422429326,-79.38355838879943,\r\n43.65602535230069,-79.3835842050612,\r\n43.656044515433045,-79.38358386978507,\r\n43.65605033714296,-79.3836029805243,\r\n43.65610321764861,-79.38362309709191,\r\n43.65612698960384,-79.38362376764417,\r\n43.65612893017122,-79.3836304731667,\r\n43.65618132546626,-79.38365226611495,\r\n43.656204369678754,-79.38365226611495,\r\n43.65620728052604,-79.38366299495101,\r\n43.656266467723185,-79.38368713483214,\r\n43.65628199222425,-79.38368679955602,\r\n43.65628635848945,-79.3837015517056,\r\n43.65633948135734,-79.38372233882546,\r\n43.65637077288764,-79.38372200354934,\r\n43.65641176719339,-79.38369417563081,\r\n43.65642826193573,-79.38361505046487,\r\n43.6564226828322,-79.38359493389726,\r\n43.6564323856206,-79.3835842050612,\r\n43.656451063483836,-79.3835030682385,\r\n43.65644427153425,-79.38348395749927,\r\n43.65645664258473,-79.38347490504384,\r\n43.65647386502332,-79.38339611515403,\r\n43.65646561765899,-79.38337096944451,\r\n43.65648017183059,-79.38336124643683,\r\n43.65649715169299,-79.38327910378575,\r\n43.656491330026434,-79.38326066359878,\r\n43.656502730789605,-79.3832509405911,\r\n43.65652092349231,-79.38317282125354,\r\n43.65651267613443,-79.3831537105143,\r\n43.65652601744808,-79.38314432278275,\r\n43.65654226958979,-79.38306352123618,\r\n43.65653596278906,-79.38302462920547,\r\n43.656551729789655,-79.38302429392934,\r\n43.656674712252304,-79.38240906223655,\r\n43.65668659811797,-79.38240906223655,\r\n43.6568088525999,-79.38183339312673,\r\n43.6567967241902,-79.3818280287087,\r\n43.65682437696073,-79.3817069940269,\r\n43.656822678983985,-79.38170531764627,\r\n43.656849846606576,-79.38158193603158,\r\n43.6568432972701,-79.38157891854644,\r\n43.6568944791027,-79.3813526071608,\r\n43.65672880505058,-79.38128219917417,\n43.65672856248208,-79.38128152862191","DETAILS":"TMU space in the Atrium on Bay is accessed from the southeast corner of the building by Dundas Square. The entrance is opposite the Eaton Centre.\n<br/><br/>\n\nTMU has two floors in the office tower where we have space for the Brookfield Institute, School of Performance, and researchers from the Department of Psychology and the Faculty of Science.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The entrance at 20 Dundas Street West has an automated door operator.<br/><br/>\n\nThere is a single-occupancy, barrier-free washroom on both TMU floors and the one on the 12th floor includes an adult change table.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.656225, -79.381789","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Atrium on Bay","CENTER":"43.65634966929921,-79.3826499581337","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"AOB","HOURS":"Monday to Friday  | 10 a.m. to 7 p.m.\r\n<br/>\r<br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. \rHours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"20 Dundas St West","ID":"121","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.65982899292453,-79.38309889286757,\r\n43.65985615918691,-79.3829419836402,\r\n43.659866346532155,-79.38294181600213,\r\n43.65993062378953,-79.38262799754739,\r\n43.65994032601108,-79.38262799754739,\r\n43.660605167008256,-79.38292656093836,\r\n43.660608562747846,-79.38293796032667,\r\n43.660702188063205,-79.38298020511866,\r\n43.66065319245006,-79.38319344073534,\r\n43.66067065623754,-79.38320148736238,\r\n43.6606197201765,-79.38342545181513,\r\n43.660601286162816,-79.38342679291964,\r\n43.66056247769442,-79.38361052423716,\r\n43.660476613868966,-79.38357498496771,\r\n43.660451388314996,-79.38357498496771,\r\n43.66044120106904,-79.38357498496771,\r\n43.66045915002503,-79.38349317759275,\r\n43.6604649713069,-79.38348898664117,\r\n43.66048874153538,-79.38337767496705,\r\n43.66037183072918,-79.38332486897707,\r\n43.66036940519136,-79.38333492726088,\r\n43.66034636257731,-79.38333643600345,\r\n43.66031749865878,-79.38332604244351,\r\n43.660321379522564,-79.38330525532365,\r\n43.65982972059244,-79.38309939578176,\r\n43.65982899292453,-79.38309889286757","DETAILS":"TMU’s College Park facility entrance is located on the west side of Yonge St. a short distance for pedestrians moving south from the Yonge and College intersection. The elevators to the TMU space can also be reached from internal building links from the College Park subway and the entrance by the College Street streetcar stop.\n<br/><br/>\nTMU’s second floor space is home to the English Language Institute (ELI) and TMU International College (TMUIC).","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance at 424 Yonge Street has an automatic door operator and a shuttle elevator off the right side of the vestibule that goes to the main floor elevator lobby. The main floor elevator has a TMU button and arrives at the office of our suite.\n<br/><br/>\nThere is a universal washroom with an adult change table in the TMU space. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.660268, -79.382831","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"English Language Institute and International College – College Park","CENTER":"43.660403362711776,-79.38308581709862","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"CPK","HOURS":"Access to Toronto MU spaces in this building is only permitted with an authorized OneCard.","ADDRESS":"424 Yonge Street","ID":"123","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.654625,-79.378782,\r\n43.65443,-79.378689,\r\n43.654528,-79.378269,\r\n43.654707,-79.378344","DETAILS":"TMU’s main SMH facilities are in theKeenan Research Centre/  Li Ka Shing Knowledge Institute building on the northeast corner of Victoria Street and Shuter Street. \n<br/><br/>\nTheBiomedical Zone and the  Institute for Biomedical Engineering, Science and Technology (iBEST) is a partnership between TMU and St. Michael’s Hospital, Unity Health Toronto","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance from Victoria Street has an automated door operator.\n<br/><br/>\nWashrooms have accessible stalls.\n<br/><br/>\nA set of elevators on the west side of the building provides access to all TMU floors.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.654507, -79.378693","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"St. Michael's Hospital","CENTER":"43.654602169415995,-79.37853075563908","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"SMH","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"209 Victoria Street","ID":"124","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.6574441,-79.3768322,\r\n43.6574965,-79.3765748,\r\n43.6576139,-79.3766230,\r\n43.6575596,-79.3768872,\r\n43.6574441,-79.3768322","DETAILS":"The MER research space is on the west side of Dalhousie Street between Dundas Street and Gould Street. It is a short distance for pedestrians travelling south from the corner by the Metro grocery store vehicle parking entrance.\n<br/><br/>\nThe research lab space is primarily occupied by the Department of Physics.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The entrance has a 30-inch door, with a barrier-free approach and an automated door operator. There is a short interior ramp from the lobby area to research spaces.\n<br/><br/>\nThere is a single-occupancy washroom with accessibility features. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\" >View washroom details</a>).","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657596, -79.376856","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Merchandise Building","CENTER":"43.6575237,-79.3767300","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"MER","HOURS":"Access to Toronto MU spaces in this building is only permitted with an authorized OneCard.","ADDRESS":"159 Dalhousie Street","ID":"125","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657914,-79.378837,\r\n43.657928,-79.378835,\r\n43.657958,-79.37871,\r\n43.657971,-79.378703,\r\n43.657977,-79.378682,\r\n43.657968,-79.378659,\r\n43.657823,-79.378592,\r\n43.657806,-79.378593,\r\n43.657801,-79.378625,\r\n43.657833,-79.378639, \r\n43.657829,-79.378656,\r\n43.657823,-79.378655,\r\n43.657812,-79.37871,\r\n43.657816,-79.378712,\r\n43.657803,-79.378771,\r\n43.657828,-79.37878,\r\n43.657825,-79.378796,","DETAILS":"O’Keefe House is on the southeast corner of Gould St. and Bond St. \n<br/><br/>\nThe historic home is the future site of the Student Wellbeing Centre. The new facility will preserve the heritage building and reimagine the historic home as a cutting-edge, purpose built wellness centre. Its valued historical components will be integrated with a modern, eight-storey addition on the south side of the property, adjacent to the Heidelberg Centre.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The building is currently slated for renovation and is not open at this time. Accessibility information will be added when the building has re-opened.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657875, -79.378721","ELEVATOR":"no","NAME":"O'Keefe House","CENTER":"43.657892,-79.378734","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/j9pI1qIQJa4","CODE":"OKF","HOURS":"Access to Toronto MU spaces in this building is only permitted with an authorized OneCard.","ADDRESS":"137 Bond Street","ID":"16","WHEELCHAIR":"no"},{"POLYGON":"43.659274,-79.377556,\r\n43.659334,-79.377554,\r\n43.659426,-79.377094,\r\n43.659448,-79.377078,\r\n43.659467,-79.376975,\r\n43.659465,-79.376934,\r\n43.659454,-79.376887,\r\n43.659435,-79.376852,\r\n43.659342,-79.376801,\r\n43.659298,-79.376803,\r\n43.659163,-79.376741,\r\n43.659102,-79.37674,\r\n43.659059,-79.376927,\r\n43.659218,-79.376997,\r\n43.659234,-79.377039,\r\n43.659138,-79.377503,","DETAILS":"PIT has a main entrance on Mutual St. a short distance for pedestrians travelling south from Gerrard St. East. The student residence also has an entrance on the west side of the building from the Pitman Quad.\n<br/><br/>\nPIT offers parking facilities for TMU community members and the garage entrance is off Mutual St. at the north end of the building.\n<br/><br/>\nThe building also is home to the Pitman Dining Hall on the west side of the building with the dining area overlooking the Pitman Quad.","ACCESSIBILITY":"All entrances have barrier-free approaches and automated door operators.\n<br/><br/>\nThere is a single-occupancy washroom with accessibility features available from the Pitman Dining Hall cafeteria.\n<br/><br/>\nElevators are near the Pitman Dining Hall entrance.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.659258, -79.376807","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Pitman Hall","CENTER":"43.659326,-79.377106","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/j9pI1qIQJa4","CODE":"PIT","HOURS":"24 hours a day, 7 days a week","ADDRESS":"160 Mutual Street","ID":"12","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.656736,-79.379099,\r\n43.656835,-79.378668,\r\n43.656753,-79.378635,\r\n43.656746,-79.378635,\r\n43.656656,-79.379043,\r\n43.656689,-79.379057,\r\n43.656684,-79.379078,\r\n43.656728,-79.3791,\r\n43.656736,-79.379099","DETAILS":"The Innovation Studio is on the west side of Bond Street mid-way between Dundas Street and Gould Street. The building is home to incubation spaces such as The Design Fabrication Zone, Fashion Zone, Music Den and Transmedia Zone. \n<br/><br/>\nThe Innovation Studio’s \"HQ\" event and exhibitions space is on the second floor.","ACCESSIBILITY":"Its entrance has a barrier-free approach and an automatic door operator. The entrance opens into a small reception area.\n<br/><br/>\nEach floor has a washroom with accessibility features. All washrooms are single-occupancy, all-gender washrooms. \n(<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nThe building’s elevator is opposite the front desk.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.656775, -79.378629","ELEVATOR":"","NAME":"Creative Innovation Studio","CENTER":"43.656759,-79.378848","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"CIS","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"110 Bond Street","ID":"144","WHEELCHAIR":""},{"POLYGON":"43.656814,-79.378898,\r\n43.656855,-79.37875,\r\n43.65682,-79.378734,\r\n43.656786,-79.378883,\r\n43.656814,-79.378898","DETAILS":"PRO is an administrative building with offices for employees that work in university operations. Access is restricted to operational personnel only.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The building was constructed in the 1860s and has original entryway features. There are stairs at the entrances and at this time there is no elevator to access the upper floors.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.656933, -79.378779","ELEVATOR":"","NAME":"114 Bond Street","CENTER":"43.656819,-79.378813","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"PRO","HOURS":"Access to Toronto MU spaces in this building is only permitted with an authorized OneCard.","ADDRESS":"114 Bond Street","ID":"143","WHEELCHAIR":""},{"POLYGON":"43.657423,-79.376798,\r\n43.657487,-79.376525,\r\n43.657419,-79.376495,\r\n43.657359,-79.376771,\r\n43.657423,-79.376798","DETAILS":"The DAL research space is on the west side of Dalhousie Street between Dundas Street and Gould Street. It is a short distance for pedestrians travelling south from the corner by the Metro grocery store vehicle parking entrance.\n<br/><br/>\nThe research lab space is primarily occupied by ECBE and Mechanical and Industrial Engineering.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The entrance has a 33-inch door, with a barrier-free approach and an automated door operator.\n<br/><br/>\nThere are two single-occupancy washrooms. Each has accessibility features.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657552, -79.376854","ELEVATOR":"","NAME":"147 Dalhousie Street","CENTER":"43.657416,-79.376651","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"DAL","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"147 Dalhousie Street","ID":"146","WHEELCHAIR":""},{"POLYGON":"43.655955,-79.38129,\r\n43.655918,-79.381281,\r\n43.655862,-79.381278,\r\n43.655748,-79.381359,\r\n43.655744,-79.381367,\r\n43.655749,-79.381384,\r\n43.655744,-79.381402,\r\n43.655734,-79.381406,\r\n43.655643,-79.38189,\r\n43.655669,-79.381959,\r\n43.65566,-79.381961,\r\n43.655614,-79.381941,\r\n43.655589,-79.381877,\r\n43.655553,-79.381898,\r\n43.655516,-79.382069,\r\n43.655495,-79.382071,\r\n43.655128,-79.381911,\r\n43.655135,-79.381886,\r\n43.65507,-79.381862,\r\n43.655058,-79.381951,\r\n43.655242,-79.382036,\r\n43.65514,-79.382466,\r\n43.655135,-79.382469,\r\n43.655026,-79.382421,\r\n43.655021,-79.382448,\r\n43.654862,-79.382565,\r\n43.65484,-79.382559,\r\n43.654836,-79.382574,\r\n43.654839,-79.382583,\r\n43.65483,-79.382632,\r\n43.654822,-79.382639,\r\n43.654816,-79.382675,\r\n43.65481,-79.382728,\r\n43.654882,-79.382758,\r\n43.654844,-79.382933,\r\n43.654772,-79.382901,\r\n43.654763,-79.38294,\r\n43.654757,-79.382945,\r\n43.654722,-79.383109,\r\n43.654638,-79.383074,\r\n43.654643,-79.383043,\r\n43.654615,-79.383031,\r\n43.654607,-79.383034,\r\n43.654589,-79.383038,\r\n43.654566,-79.383038,\r\n43.654549,-79.383033,\r\n43.654531,-79.383015,\r\n43.654521,-79.382989,\r\n43.654479,-79.382976,\r\n43.654489,-79.382926,\r\n43.654488,-79.382925,\r\n43.654612,-79.38235,\r\n43.654639,-79