81041,\r\n43.656169,-79.381186,\r\n43.656097,-79.38122,\r\n43.655955,-79.38129","DETAILS":"TMU has research space in the Galleria Offices of the Toronto Eaton Centre. The nearest entrance is on Yonge St. near a crosswalk north of Shuter St. (by Roots clothing store). The elevator to the Galleria Offices is by Indigo Books’ upper entrance on Level 4.\n<br/><br/>\nTEC provides research space for Electrical, Computer and Biomedical Engineering, the Canada Excellence Research Chair in Migration and Integration and Toronto Metropolitan Centre for Immigration and Settlement.","ACCESSIBILITY":"For an accessible route to the Level 4 elevator to Galleria Offices, enter the Eaton Centre by Roots and travel south using the ramp by Indigo Books, then take the elevator (nearest Sephora, across the corridor from Indigo) up to P1. Use the mezzanine exit from the elevator vestibule and cross the bridge from Parking toward Indigo Books.\n<br/><br/>\nThere is an all-gender washroom with accessibility features near the elevator lobby.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.654731, -79.380547","ELEVATOR":"","NAME":"Toronto Eaton Centre","CENTER":"43.654863,-79.380803","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"TEC","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"220 Yonge Street","ID":"147","WHEELCHAIR":""},{"POLYGON":"43.7483703,-79.4758705,\r\n43.7480951,-79.4757470,\r\n43.7481610,-79.4755216,\r\n43.7484323,-79.4756611,\r\n43.7483703,-79.4758705","DETAILS":"TMU’s aerospace facility is part of the Downsview Aerospace Innovation and Research Hub, located in the northeast region of Downsview Park and across the street from the Centennial College Downsview Campus.\n<br/><br/>\nThe TMU facility is 80 metres from the TTC bus stop \"Carl Hall Rd at Centennial College\" for the 101 Downsview Park route that operates between the Sheppard West Station and Downsview Park subway station.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The building is a former WWII aviation hangar and was not built as an AODA-compliant structure. Entrance doors are 30” or less and the south door has a step up to enter. The second floor can only be accessed by stairs.\n<br/><br/>\nThere is a single-occupancy washroom that is not currently AODA compliant.\n<br/><br/>\nThe TTC bus route #101 offers accessible service and stops near TMU’s facility and provides service to Sheppard West Station and Downsview Station which are both accessible subway stations.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.748254, -79.475585","ELEVATOR":"","NAME":"Downsview","CENTER":"43.7482424,-79.4756987","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"DWV","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"60 Carl Hall Road","ID":"150","WHEELCHAIR":""},{"POLYGON":"43.686526,-79.758889,\r\n43.686522,-79.758891,\r\n43.686369,-79.759057,\r\n43.686442,-79.759191,\r\n43.686606,-79.759011,\r\n43.686526,-79.758889","DETAILS":"33 Queen Street, Brampton, Ontario","ACCESSIBILITY":"","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"","ELEVATOR":"","NAME":"Brampton City Hall","CENTER":"43.68648,-79.75905","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"BRU","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"33 Queen Street, Brampton, Ontario","ID":"151","WHEELCHAIR":""},{"POLYGON":"43.686898,-79.761631,\r\n43.686955,-79.761541,\r\n43.687031,-79.761644,\r\n43.686957,-79.761724,\r\n43.686898,-79.761631","DETAILS":"1 Nelson Street West, Brampton, Ontario","ACCESSIBILITY":"","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"","ELEVATOR":"","NAME":"Rogers Cybersecure Catalyst","CENTER":"43.686966,-79.761637","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"CSC","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"1 Nelson Street West, Brampton, Ontario","ID":"152","WHEELCHAIR":""},{"POLYGON":"43.65999,-79.377446,\r\n43.660025,-79.377302,\r\n43.660035,-79.377297,\r\n43.66007,-79.377188,\r\n43.660052,-79.37718,\r\n43.660055,-79.377166,\r\n43.660066,-79.37713,\r\n43.660062,-79.377129,\r\n43.66007,-79.377106,\r\n43.660049,-79.377097,\r\n43.660052,-79.377082,\r\n43.660001,-79.377064,\r\n43.66001,-79.377055,\r\n43.660004,-79.377033,\r\n43.660012,-79.376996,\r\n43.659997,-79.376991,\r\n43.659997,-79.376971,\r\n43.659897,-79.376907,\r\n43.659878,-79.376909,\r\n43.659872,-79.376921,\r\n43.659858,-79.37691,\r\n43.659841,-79.376876,\r\n43.659713,-79.37683,\r\n43.659694,-79.37683,\r\n43.65969,-79.376841,\r\n43.659666,-79.37683,\r\n43.659646,-79.376827,\r\n43.659642,-79.376847,\r\n43.659616,-79.376854,\r\n43.659626,-79.376917,\r\n43.659578,-79.376897,\r\n43.659538,-79.376895,\r\n43.659537,-79.376906,\r\n43.659526,-79.376905,\r\n43.659491,-79.376893,\r\n43.659439,-79.377155,\r\n43.659445,-79.377157,\r\n43.659432,-79.377216,\r\n43.659457,-79.377223","DETAILS":"SHE is a two story addition that was added to the top of Eric Palin Hall (EPH) and its entrance is on the south side of Gerrard St. East at the corner by Mutual St. \n<br/><br/>\nSHE facilities are on the 5th and 6th floors of the building where the principal residents are the Faculty of Community Services and several of its schools and George Brown College.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance has a barrier-free approach and an automated door operator. An elevator from the main entrance also serves as a shuttle to bypass stairs leading to the 2nd floor alternate entrance to EPH and the main elevator lobby.\n<br/><br/>\nThere are single-occupancy, all-gender washrooms with accessibility features available on each floor. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nElevators from the main elevator lobby serve the 5th and 6th floors.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.659951, -79.377189","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Sally Horsfall Eaton Centre for Studies in Community Health","CENTER":"43.659757,-79.377165","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/3I9LwBZx2zI","CODE":"SHE","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 6 a.m. to 10 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday | 7 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/>\nSunday | 7:30 a.m. to 4 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"99 Gerrard Street East","ID":"10","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.65802726015412,-79.38098128885031,\r\n43.65796225316858,-79.38124548643827,\r\n43.657924413249056,-79.38125688582659,\r\n43.65790549328036,-79.38133802264929,\r\n43.657828357961655,-79.38139166682959,\r\n43.65754940865493,-79.38123140484095,\r\n43.65761975251532,-79.3809263035655,\r\n43.65771192710422,-79.38084784895182,\r\n43.65778275590273,-79.38087936490774,\r\n43.65780652719308,-79.38078749924898,\r\n43.65784776308259,-79.38080292195082,\r\n43.65782253642413,-79.38089679926634,\r\n43.65802823040708,-79.38098128885031,\r\n43.65802726015412,-79.38098128885031","DETAILS":"Located on the northeast corner of the Yonge and Gould St. intersection, the SLC is the symbolic “front door” of TMU. The School of Performance has a separate box-office entrance at 345 Yonge St. \n<br/><br/>\nThe main SLC building can also be reached via the Library Building (LIB) using a pedestrian bridge from the University Library on the 2nd floor.\n<br/><br/>\nIn addition to the School of Performance on the Lower Level, the SLC provides facilities for Student Life & Learning Support, Academic Accommodation Support and the DMZ.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance can be reached by a set of concrete stairs or an accessibility ramp from the Gould St. sidewalk. A passenger elevator is also available at the southeast corner of the building by O’Keefe Lane and serves as a shuttle to the main entrance level.\nThe School of Performance has a separate barrier-free box-office entrance at 345 Yonge St. \n<br/><br/>\nThere is a single-occupancy, all-gender washroom with accessibility features on each floor. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nFour elevators serve the main SLC building’s floors 1 through 8.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657602, -79.381217","ELEVATOR":"","NAME":"Sheldon & Tracy Levy Student Learning Centre","CENTER":"43.657679,-79.38112","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"SLC","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 7 a.m. to 8:30 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"341 Yonge Street","ID":"82","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657061,-79.379753,\r\n43.657122,-79.379752,\r\n43.657204,-79.37938,\r\n43.656803,-79.379211,\r\n43.656769,-79.37921,\r\n43.656689,-79.379575,\r\n43.656659,-79.379585,\r\n43.656659,-79.379585","DETAILS":"VIC is on the east side of Victoria St. with its entrance 65 metres north of Dundas St. It is opposite TMU’s Parking Garage. \n<br/><br/>\nThe building has several classrooms and has the TMU Security kiosk to the right of the main entrance lobby as you enter. The Faculty of Science and Facilities Management and Development are on the building’s upper floors.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance has a barrier-free approach and an automated door operator. \n<br/><br/>\nThe building also has a rear entrance with an automated door operator in the laneway on the east side of the building.\n<br/><br/>\nWomen’s washrooms have stalls with accessibility features on the 1st, 3rd and 5th floors. Men’s washrooms have stalls with accessibility features on the 2nd, 4th, and 6th floors.\n<br/><br/>\nThere are five elevators in the main lobby that provide access to floors 1 through 8. An accessible lift to the basement level is in the first-floor corridor.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657021, -79.379740","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Victoria Building","CENTER":"43.656959,-79.379482","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"VIC","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 7 a.m. to 10:30 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday | 7 a.m. to 7 p.m.<br/>\nSunday | Card access only<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"285 Victoria Street","ID":"15","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.6602908,-79.3801069,\r\n43.6601846,-79.3800662,\r\n43.6601870,-79.3800541,\r\n43.6601870,-79.3800541,\r\n43.6601283,-79.3800280,\r\n43.6601230,-79.3800085,\r\n43.6601230,-79.3800085,\r\n43.6601341,-79.3799723,\r\n43.6601167,-79.3799609,\r\n43.6601108,-79.3799736,\r\n43.6597077,-79.3798038,\r\n43.6597882,-79.3794401,\r\n43.6601070,-79.3795717,\r\n43.6601021,-79.3796126,\r\n43.6601220,-79.3796193,\r\n43.6601016,-79.3797200,\r\n43.6600813,-79.3797112,\r\n43.6600754,-79.3797294,\r\n43.6600080,-79.3797005,\r\n43.6599998,-79.3797314,\r\n43.6600662,-79.3797609,\r\n43.6600648,-79.3797683,\r\n43.6600982,-79.3797716,\r\n43.6601138,-79.3797804,\r\n43.6601089,-79.3797851,\r\n43.6601351,-79.3797857,\r\n43.6601511,-79.3797944,\r\n43.6601487,-79.3798119,\r\n43.6601686,-79.3798186,\r\n43.6601749,-79.3797918,\r\n43.6602418,-79.3798186,\r\n43.6603393,-79.3798609,\r\n43.6603418,-79.3798730,\r\n43.6602908,-79.3801069","DETAILS":"Located on the north side of Gerrard St., a short distance for pedestrians moving westward from the Church St. intersection. The main entrance is at 44 Gerrard St. East, one of two entrances fronting Gerrard. \n<br/><br/>\nA courtyard bicycle parking facility can be accessed via a gate from McGill St. A secondary entrance to the building’s second floor is also on McGill St.\n<br/><br/>\nCUI is the home of several research programs, including: Centre for Urban Energy, Clean Energy Zone, Food Research, Science Discovery Zone and Urban Water TMU.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance at 44 Gerrard St. East has a barrier-free approach and automatic door operator. There are internal ramps at the entrance.\n<br/><br/>\nAll washrooms in the building are single-occupancy, all-gender facilities. Each floor has a washroom with accessibility features. There are two baby change tables in washrooms on the 1st and 2nd floor, and an adult change table in a 3rd floor washroom. \n(<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nThere is an elevator centrally located in the building.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.659738, -79.379717","ELEVATOR":"no","NAME":"Centre for Urban Innovation","CENTER":"43.659806,-79.379686","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/-8Rrs3VbYBM","CODE":"CUI","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"44 Gerrard Street East","ID":"23","WHEELCHAIR":"no"},{"POLYGON":"43.658102,-79.377662,\r\n43.658134,-79.377659,\r\n43.658157,-79.377597,\r\n43.658163,-79.377597,\r\n43.65822,-79.377348,\r\n43.658215,-79.377345,\r\n43.65823,-79.377268,\t\r\n43.657083,-79.376758,\r\n43.657052,-79.376756,\t\r\n43.65701,-79.376938, \t\r\n43.657028,-79.376948,\r\n43.657007,-79.377034,\r\n43.656991,-79.377034,\r\n43.656971,-79.37713,\r\n43.657078,-79.377194,\r\n43.657436,-79.377365,\r\n43.657595,-79.377422,\r\n43.657743,-79.377486,\r\n43.657741,-79.377503,\r\n43.657833,-79.377529,\r\n43.657961,-79.3776,\r\n43.657993,-79.377599,","DETAILS":"ENG is on the east side of Church St. and spans almost the full length of the block from Gould St. to just north of Dundas St. Its main entrance is at the centre point of the building’s Church St. façade. The most-used entrance is the north entrance at the Church-Gould intersection. \n<br/><br/>\nThe building provides facilities for Computer Science, Mathematics, Aerospace Engineering, Civil Engineering and Electrical, Computer and Biomedical Engineering. It also has the administrative offices for the Faculty of Engineering and Architectural Science.","ACCESSIBILITY":"Both the main and north entrances have barrier-free approaches (the north entrance has a ramp along the building face) and automated door operators.\n<br/><br/>\nThere are single-occupancy washrooms with accessibility features on all floors, except the Lower Ground floor, which has washrooms with stalls that have accessibility features. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nThe elevator lobby is in the centre section of the building opposite the Church St. main entrance.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.658112, -79.377632","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"George Vari Engineering and Computing Centre","CENTER":"43.657572,-79.377229","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/mvYhrvZtHMw","CODE":"ENG","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 7 a.m. to 9 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday | 7 a.m. to 5:30 p.m.<br/>\nSunday | 7 a.m. to 5 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change","ADDRESS":"245 Church Street","ID":"4","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.659393,-79.378864,\r\n43.659422,-79.378859,\r\n43.659717,-79.37867,\r\n43.659199,-79.378445,\r\n43.659202,-79.378427,\r\n43.659135,-79.378399,\r\n43.659137,-79.378387,\r\n43.659167,-79.378385,\r\n43.659181,-79.378318,\r\n43.659077,-79.378273,\r\n43.659064,-79.378273,\r\n43.659063,-79.3783,\r\n43.659061,-79.378292,\r\n43.659056,-79.378293,\r\n43.65905,-79.378296,\r\n43.659047,-79.378315,\r\n43.659041,-79.378314,\r\n43.659046,-79.378276,\r\n43.65902,-79.378277,\r\n43.659019,-79.378286,\r\n43.658986,-79.378272,\r\n43.658979,-79.378272,\r\n43.65897,-79.378321,\r\n43.658937,-79.378306,\r\n43.65891,-79.378306,\r\n43.658571,-79.378165,\r\n43.658572,-79.378155,\r\n43.658617,-79.378152,\r\n43.658542,-79.378002,\r\n43.658523,-79.378,\r\n43.658483,-79.378013,\r\n43.658506,-79.377924,\r\n43.658538,-79.377786,\r\n43.658514,-79.377774,\r\n43.658476,-79.377906,\r\n43.658431,-79.378055,\r\n43.658425,-79.377945,\r\n43.658315,-79.377947,\r\n43.658269,-79.377972,\r\n43.65826,-79.378022,\r\n43.658195,-79.378079,\r\n43.658181,-79.378112,\r\n43.658216,-79.37814,\r\n43.658233,-79.378173,\r\n43.658247,-79.378171,\r\n43.658262,-79.378161,\n43.658281,-79.378152,\r\n43.65829,-79.378079,\r\n43.658308,-79.378083,\r\n43.658469,-79.378458,\r\n43.658467,-79.37847,\r\n43.65873,-79.378573,\r\n43.658724,-79.3786,\r\n43.659093,-79.378748,\r\n43.659117,-79.378748,\r\n43.659134,-79.37874","DETAILS":"KHE runs along the west side of Church St. for the full block between Gerrard St. East and Gould St. Its entrance is on Church St. at the north end of the building by Gerrard. \n<br/><br/>\nThe building has internal links to Kerr Hall North (KHN), Kerr Hall South (KHS) and a second-floor pedestrian bridge to the Rogers Communications Centre (RCC). All sections of Kerr Hall can be accessed via the second floor.\n<br/><br/>\nThe building holds many general-use classrooms and — along with Kerr Hall North — houses several chemistry, biology and physics labs as well as some facilities for chemical, civil, mechanical, industrial and aerospace engineering. The Department of Physics has its offices on the 3rd floor.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The entrance is accessed by a ramp at the corner and it has an automated door operator.\n<br/><br/>\nThere are some single-occupancy washrooms with accessibility features in Kerr Hall North accessible from corridors shared with KHE on the 1st, 2nd and 3rd floors. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nKHE shares an elevator with KHS at the south end of the building.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.659630, -79.378649","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Kerr Hall East","CENTER":"43.65901,-79.378535","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/Rx4mqpVCHh4","CODE":"KHE","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 6 a.m. to 10:30 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday | 8 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"340 Church Street","ID":"35","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.659059,-79.380083,\r\n43.659081,-79.380091,\r\n43.659286,-79.380593,\r\n43.659376,-79.380172,\r\n43.659382,-79.380182,\r\n43.6594,-79.380182,\r\n43.659433,-79.380168,\r\n43.659449,-79.380111,\r\n43.65944,-79.380107,\r\n43.659423,-79.380107,\r\n43.659414,-79.380122,\r\n43.659409,-79.380125,\r\n43.659394,-79.380088,\r\n43.65943,-79.37992,\r\n43.659451,-79.379936,\r\n43.659466,-79.379939,\r\n43.659491,-79.379895,\r\n43.659494,-79.379828,\r\n43.659455,-79.379818,\r\n43.659452,-79.379818,\r\n43.659717,-79.37867,\r\n43.659422,-79.378859,\r\n43.659393,-79.378864,\r\n43.659223,-79.379666,\r\n43.659186,-79.379652,\r\n43.659179,-79.37965,\r\n43.659168,-79.379726,\r\n43.659199,-79.379776,\r\n43.659169,-79.379916,\r\n43.659159,-79.379874,\r\n43.659101,-79.379878,\r\n43.659107,-79.379938,\r\n43.659104,-79.379938,\r\n43.659097,-79.379955,\r\n43.659092,-79.37996","DETAILS":"KHN is on the south side of Gerrard St. East between Nelson Mandela Walk (formerly Victoria St.) and Church St. It has two distinct sections separated by an archway to the Kerr Hall Quad at its centre. The entrances at 31 Gerrard St. East and 340 Church St. access each half respectively.\r\nBoth sections of the building can also be accessed from entrances in the Kerr Hall Quad.\r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe east section of the building has laboratory facilities and the administrative offices of the Department of Chemistry and Biology. The west half of the building holds The Theatre at the Creative School, the accessible entrance to the Recreation and Athletics Centre and access to TMU’s Medical Centre. \r\n<br/><br/>\r\nThe Theatre has a public entrance under the archway at 43 Gerrard St. East when performances are scheduled.\r\nKHN shares corridors with Kerr Hall East, Kerr Hall West and the western half can be accessed from a pedestrian bridge from Jorgenson Hall on the second and third floors.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The 31 Gerrard St. East entrance by the west corner has a barrier-free approach and automated door operator. This entrance does not provide access to the eastern half of KHN. The eastern half of KHN is accessed via 340 Church St. which has an accessible ramp and an automated door operator. \n<br/><br/>\nSingle-occupancy accessible washrooms are available on the 1st, 2nd and 3rd floors of the eastern section of KHN. KHN-W has a “staff only” washroom on the 3rd floor. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nKHN has an elevator by the 31 Gerrard St. East entrance. The eastern half of the building relies on the KHE elevator at the southeast corner of Kerr Hall.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.659385, -79.379529","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Kerr Hall North","CENTER":"43.659365,-79.379582","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/whBWjFQnYbU","CODE":"KHN","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 6 a.m. to 10:30 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday | 8 a.m. to 6 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"43 Gerrard Street East","ID":"34","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.65806,-79.380911,\r\n43.6581,-79.380912,\r\n43.658109,-79.380842,\r\n43.65813,-79.380841,\r\n43.658218,-79.380429,\r\n43.658222,-79.380402,\r\n43.658093,-79.380344,\r\n43.658152,-79.380117,\r\n43.658078,-79.380083,\r\n43.65805,-79.380084,\r\n43.658008,-79.380283,\r\n43.65782,-79.380197,\r\n43.657773,-79.380198,\r\n43.65766,-79.380674,\r\n43.657799,-79.380737,\r\n43.657796,-79.380778,\r\n43.658059,-79.380898","DETAILS":"The main entrance to the Library Building (LIB) is just north of the pedestrianized intersection of Gould St. and Nelson Mandela Walk (formerly Victoria St.). The main doors open into a Lower Ground floor lobby that links the building to the Podium (POD).\n<br/><br/>\nThe University Library is the main occupant of the building and its interior entrance is on the 2nd floor of LIB. The University Library also has an entrance via a pedestrian bridge from the 2nd floor of the Student Learning Centre (SLC) at 341 Yonge St.\n<br/><br/>\nThe interior entrance to the University Library can be accessed by a set of \"scissor stairs\" from the Lower Ground lobby, the pedestrian bridge from the 2nd floor of KHW, or the LIB accessible elevator.","ACCESSIBILITY":"An entrance with accessibility features is south of the main entrance and can be reached by a ramp from Gould St. across the street from the Campus Store.\n<br/><br/>\nSingle-occupancy washrooms with accessibility features are available on floors 1, 2, 4, and 7. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nThe LIB accessible elevator travels between the Basement Level through the 4th floor. The University Library has an additional elevator bank inside its facilities to access all floors of the library stacks, study areas and Archives and Special Collections.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.658027, -79.380433","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Library Building","CENTER":"43.657836,-79.380587","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/UrPWgULe0co","CODE":"LIB","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 7 a.m. to 1 a.m.<br/>\nSaturday and Sunday | 10 a.m. to 1 a.m. <br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"350 Victoria Street","ID":"1","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.659634,-79.378301,\r\n43.659791,-79.37836,\r\n43.659816,-79.378362,\r\n43.659906,-79.377967,\r\n43.659759,-79.377907,\r\n43.659728,-79.377906,\r\n43.659712,-79.377985,\r\n43.659716,-79.37799,","DETAILS":"MON is on the southeast corner of the Gerrard-Church St. intersection. The building’s entrance is on the east side of the building in the laneway facing Eric Palin Hall (EPH). \n<br/><br/>\nThe building is home to research space, classrooms and the administrative offices of the Department of Civil Engineering.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance has a barrier-free approach and an automated door operator. \n<br/><br/>\nAll washrooms are single-occupancy. Each floor has an all-gender, single-occupancy washroom with accessibility features. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nAn elevator is to the left as you enter the main corridor.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.659813, -79.377934","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Civil Engineering Building – Monetary Times","CENTER":"43.65978,-79.378136","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/TE0f5EBgvNk","CODE":"MON","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 8 a.m. to 4:30 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"341 Church Street","ID":"14","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657895,-79.378224,\r\n43.657865,-79.378209,\r\n43.657927,-79.37792,\r\n43.658051,-79.377972,\r\n43.657974,-79.378291,\r\n43.657979,-79.378296,\r\n43.657969,-79.378341,\r\n43.657878,-79.378306,\r\n43.657895,-79.378224","DETAILS":"Oakham House is located at the southwest corner of Gould St. and Church St. The heritage building is integrated with the Student Campus Centre (SCC) and its spaces are primarily accessed from the SCC.\n<br/><br/>\nOAK houses the Oakham Café, event and meeting facilities on the 1st and 2nd floors, a multi-faith room on the 3rd floor and the Met Campus Pub on the basement level. The pub has a main entrance from the Church St. terrace.","ACCESSIBILITY":"Although the main entrance has an accessibility ramp, door operator and a shuttle elevator to bypass interior stairs, spaces are primarily accessed from the adjoining SCC where the approach is barrier-free and the interior elevator and ramp configurations are more user friendly.\n<br/><br/>\nWashroom facilities are all single-occupancy, all-gender washrooms. There are washrooms with accessibility features on each floor. OAK-125 has an adult change table and a baby change table. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nThe building shares the SCC elevator.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657949, -79.378402","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Oakham House","CENTER":"43.657976,-79.378004","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"OAK","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 6 a.m. to 11 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"63 Gould Street","ID":"19","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.657483,-79.380129,\r\n43.657007,-79.379906,\r\n43.656948,-79.380228,\r\n43.657418,-79.380425,","DETAILS":"The Victoria Street Parking garage offers permit parking for TMU community members and hourly rates for the general public. The vehicle entrance is off Victoria St. north of Dundas St. on the west side of the street.\n<br/><br/>\nPedestrian access is approximately 25 metres north of the vehicle entrance. Payment machines are on the 3rd floor and next to the attendant kiosk. You can also pay by credit card on exit.","ACCESSIBILITY":"Dedicated accessible parking spaces are available on the P1 level.\n<br/><br/>\nThe pedestrian access has a barrier-free approach and automated door operator. It opens to an elevator lobby.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657274, -79.380062","ELEVATOR":"no","NAME":"Parking Garage","CENTER":"43.657285,-79.380188","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"PKG","HOURS":"24 hours a day, 7 days a week","ADDRESS":"300 Victoria Street","ID":"22","WHEELCHAIR":"no"},{"POLYGON":"43.65806,-79.380911,\r\n43.6581,-79.380912,\r\n43.658109,-79.380842,\r\n43.65813,-79.380841,\r\n43.658218,-79.380429,\r\n43.658222,-79.380431,\r\n43.658228,-79.380412,\r\n43.658235,-79.380413,\r\n43.658248,-79.380417,\r\n43.658248,-79.380433,\r\n43.658234,-79.380438,\r\n43.658235,-79.380452,\r\n43.658353,-79.380505,\r\n43.658337,-79.380535,\r\n43.658359,-79.380537,\r\n43.658359,-79.380548,\r\n43.658739,-79.380724,\r\n43.658744,-79.380723,\r\n43.658754,-79.380659,\r\n43.65877,-79.380659,\r\n43.658893,-79.380714,\r\n43.658947,-79.380464,\r\n43.658967,-79.380464,\r\n43.659048,-79.380505,\r\n43.658987,-79.380764,\r\n43.658962,-79.380906,\r\n43.658905,-79.381128,\r\n43.658959,-79.38115,\n43.658958,-79.381159,\r\n43.658992,-79.381176,\r\n43.658975,-79.381243,\r\n43.658964,-79.381245,\r\n43.658958,-79.381242,\r\n43.658945,-79.381284,\n43.658904,-79.381286,\r\n43.658875,-79.381274,\r\n43.658873,-79.381263,\r\n43.658857,-79.381263,\r\n43.65806,-79.380911","DETAILS":"POD is a four-story building along Nelson Mandela Walk that connects Jorgenson Hall (JOR) to the north to the Library Building (LIB) to the south. The building does not have its own main entrance, but shares the entry lobbies and elevators of LIB and JOR.\n<br/><br/>\nIt holds key student services such as the ServiceHub, OneCard office, Campus Tours, Hub Café and other student-support services. The Lincoln Alexander School of Law and Law Library are on the 4th floor.\n<br/><br/>\nPOD also has event and exhibition spaces.","ACCESSIBILITY":"POD relies on the Library Building (LIB) and Jorgenson Hall (JOR) entrances, which have doors with accessibility features.\n<br/><br/>\nSingle-occupancy washrooms with accessibility features are available on the 4th floor of POD and the 1st and 2nd floors of LIB near the accessible lift. Washrooms with accessible stalls are on the Lower Ground level of LIB. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nPassenger elevators in LIB and JOR provide access to POD floors.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.658027, -79.380433","ELEVATOR":"no","NAME":"Podium","CENTER":"43.658488,-79.380823","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/q8ExbI39Ajc","CODE":"POD","HOURS":"Monday to Sunday | 5 a.m. to 1 a.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"350 Victoria Street","ID":"5","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.647783,-79.394617\r\n,\r\n43.647766,-79.394609,\r\n43.647846,-79.394231,\r\n43.647752,-79.394193,\r\n43.647757,-79.394163,\r\n43.647729,-79.394164,\r\n43.647725,-79.39418,\r\n43.647679,-79.394159,\r\n43.647668,-79.394157,\r\n43.647632,-79.394348,\r\n43.647585,-79.394333,\r\n43.647576,-79.394333,\r\n43.647556,-79.394436,\r\n43.647608,-79.394459,\r\n43.647527,-79.394845,\r\n43.647594,-79.394865,\r\n43.647588,-79.3949,\r\n43.647717,-79.394957,\r\n43.647783,-79.394617","DETAILS":"RCD is a heritage-designated, industrial arts building located on Richmond St. just east of Spadina Ave. The building is home to a cafe, art galleries, studios and the student and Artspace, a TMU student- and faculty-run gallery space.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The main entrance has an accessibility ramp leading to an automated door at the café entrance, which connects internally to the main building. A secondary entrance close to the corner of Richmond St. and Peter St. has ramp access and an automated door operator. \n<br/><br/>\nAn elevator serves all floors of the building including the lower level and the TMU gallery.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.647778, -79.395134","ELEVATOR":"","NAME":"401 Richmond Street West","CENTER":"43.647725,-79.394535","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"RCD","HOURS":"","ADDRESS":"401 Richmond Street West","ID":"148","WHEELCHAIR":""},{"POLYGON":"43.65702,-79.378484,\n43.657109,-79.378047,\r\n43.657109,-79.378039,\r\n43.656746,-79.37788,\r\n43.656726,-79.377873,\r\n43.656627,-79.378307,","DETAILS":"SBB is on the east side of Bond St. a short distance for pedestrians travelling north from Dundas St. Its main entrance is a few metres north of the loading doors of TMU’s Shipping and Receiving. \n<br/><br/>\nThe building is home to psychology research labs on the 1st and 2nd floors and the School of Urban and Regional Planning on the 3rd and 4th floors.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The entrance has a barrier-free approach and automated door operator. Once inside there is an interior ramp to the main lobby.\n<br/><br/>\nThere is a single-occupancy washroom with accessibility features on each floor. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\" >View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nThe passenger elevator is in the main lobby opposite the entrance.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.656742, -79.378354","ELEVATOR":"no","NAME":"South Bond Building","CENTER":"43.656891,-79.378197","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/izDo-Uc21jM","CODE":"SBB","HOURS":"Monday to Friday | 8 a.m. to 10 p.m.<br/>\nSaturday | 8 a.m. to 4 p.m.<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"105 Bond Street","ID":"21","WHEELCHAIR":"no"},{"POLYGON":"43.657557,-79.378173,\r\n43.657626,-79.377929,\r\n43.65781,-79.378009,\r\n43.657805,-79.37803,\r\n43.657831,-79.378042,\r\n43.657864,-79.377894,\r\n43.657873,-79.377895,\r\n43.657929,-79.377919,\r\n43.657867,-79.37821,\r\n43.657895,-79.378224,\r\n43.657879,-79.378305,\r\n43.657965,-79.37834,\r\n43.657956,-79.378394,\r\n43.657911,-79.378602,\r\n43.657903,-79.378603,\r\n43.657694,-79.378513,\r\n43.657736,-79.378321,\r\n43.65771,-79.378309,\r\n43.657711,-79.378304,\r\n43.657687,-79.378291,\r\n43.657708,-79.378203,\r\n43.657689,-79.378195,\r\n43.657664,-79.378172,\r\n43.657663,-79.378172,\r\n43.657648,-79.378164,\r\n43.657645,-79.378164,\r\n43.657557,-79.378173","DETAILS":"The SCC is on the south side of Gould St. mid-way between Bond St. and Church St. The building is integrated with the adjoining Oakham House (OAK) on the east side.\n<br/><br/>\nThe building is home to TMU's two main students' unions, their affiliated campus groups and course unions.","ACCESSIBILITY":"The SCC's main entrance has a barrier-free approach and an automated door operator. \n<br/><br/>\nWashrooms have stalls with accessibility features on each floor. Adjoining facilities of Oakham House offer single-occupancy washrooms with accessibility features. OAK-125 has an adult change table and a baby change table. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).\n<br/><br/>\nThe elevator is in the southern half of the building on the west side of the main corridor space.","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.657949, -79.378402","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Student Campus Centre","CENTER":"43.65783,-79.378409","VIDEO_REF":"http://www.youtube.com/embed/5PnVfmibcR4","CODE":"SCC","HOURS":"Monday and Thursday | 6 a.m. to 9 p.m.<br/>\nTuesday and Wednesday | 6 a.m. to 8 p.m. <br/>\nThursday | 6 a.m. to 9 p.m.<br/>\nFriday to Sunday | 6 a.m. to 11 p.m<br/><br/>\nOutside of these hours, entry is only permitted with an authorized OneCard. Hours are subject to change.","ADDRESS":"55 Gould Street","ID":"17","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"},{"POLYGON":"43.655626,-79.38188,\r\n43.655694,-79.382044,\r\n43.655718,-79.382061,\r\n43.655891,-79.382056,\r\n43.656116,-79.381904,\r\n43.656177,-79.381597,\r\n43.656057,-79.381289,\r\n43.656025,-79.381279,\r\n43.655881,-79.381278,\r\n43.655767,-79.381372,\r\n43.65577,-79.381388,\r\n43.655765,-79.381411,\r\n43.655737,-79.381407,\r\n43.655727,-79.381454,\r\n43.655714,-79.381447","DETAILS":"YDI is an office tower abutting the Eaton Centre on the south side of Dundas St. The entrance is 65 metres west of the Yonge-Dundas intersection. The building has internal links to the Yonge-Dundas subway station and the PATH via the Eaton Centre.\r\n\r<br/><br/>\nTMU has administrative offices on several floors of the building. \r\n<br/><br/>\nThere are two sets of elevators. The eastern set of elevators accesses TMU spaces on floors 4, 9, 10 and 11. The western set of elevators accesses the TMU space on the 16th floor.\r\n<br/><br/>\nAccess to the 16th floor requires a Cadillac Fairview access","ACCESSIBILITY":"The building has a barrier-free approach and the set of doors west of the revolving doors has an automated door operator.\n<br/><br/>\nThere is a single-occupancy, all-gender washroom on each floor with a TMU space. (<a href=\"https://www.torontomu.ca/facilities-management-development/facilities-help-desk/accessibility-amenity-information/single-occupancy-washrooms/\" target=\"_blank\">View washroom details</a>).","DEFAULT_ENTRANCE":"43.656025, -79.381557","ELEVATOR":"yes","NAME":"Yonge-Dundas Intersection","CENTER":"43.656043,-79.38173","VIDEO_REF":"","CODE":"YDI","HOURS":"Access to Toronto MU spaces in this building is only permitted with an authorized OneCard.","ADDRESS":"1 Dundas Street West","ID":"32","WHEELCHAIR":"yes"}]